cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  ATLAS: Analysis and Testing of Language Models for Archival Systems
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the specific release you ran. The
  version matters: release notes record the study design a given version
  implements, and those have changed between versions.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Smithies
    given-names: James
    affiliation: Australian National University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4801-0366"
  - family-names: Berman
    given-names: Glen
    affiliation: Australian National University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3249-0190"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AI-as-Infrastructure/aiinfra-atlas"
url: "https://aiinfra.anu.edu.au"
abstract: >-
  A test harness for evaluating Large Language Model Retrieval Augmented
  Generation (RAG) for Humanities and Social Science research, including an
  inter-rater reliability workflow for structured expert evaluation of generated
  responses. A deliverable of the AI as Infrastructure (AIINFRA) project. The
  default corpus is 1901 parliamentary records from Australia, Aotearoa New
  Zealand and the United Kingdom, but the vector store is designed to be
  replaceable.
keywords:
  - retrieval augmented generation
  - large language models
  - digital humanities
  - inter-rater reliability
  - evaluation framework
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-10-30"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.17204351
    description: >-
      Zenodo concept DOI, resolving to the latest release. Each release also has
      its own version DOI, listed in ReadMe.md under "Major Releases"; cite that
      one for the version you ran.
# Authorship reflects project contribution, not commit counts: the git history
# has a single committer, so the author list cannot be derived from it.
